WEBVTT

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.810
Amazing, Yabuki Joe.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.770
You truly are an amazing man.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:29.570
Now I can finally say this to myself:

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.480
I am burning as bright as I can.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.040
It's Carlos Rivera vs. Yabuki Joe,

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.500
and after an intense exchange of downs in the first round,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.300
the audience filling Korakuen Hall are on the edge of their seats!

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.300
What we are showing you on the screen right now

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:58.470
is the intense body blow off the ropes that Yabuki showed us at the end of the first round!

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.890
Now isn't that something, Ishida-san?

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:03.220
Yes, I never expected Yabuki to come up with a strategy like that!

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.020
Either way, they're about evenly matched at this point.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.230
Anything could happen now.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.780
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.290
Hooray! Hooray! Yabuki!

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.250
Now listen, Joe!

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.250
Carlos should still be reeling from his past down!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.290
Give it all you got!

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.800
Carlos, be careful of the ropes!

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.560
Fight!

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.940
Now then, what will Yabuki do? And what will Carlos do?

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.770
Both of them have stern, serious expressions!

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:51.170
Way to go, you two! That was intense!

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.160
<i>Yeah, way to go!</i>

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.460
Joe, the ropes! Use the ropes!

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.220
Now that was a breathtaking exchange of blows!

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.630
Both of them have thrown themselves into an astounding fistfight!

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.800
Now they've stepped back to catch their breath...

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:03.630
Oh, Yabuki goes for it!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.390
But Carlos sways!

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.060
Yabuki throws a right! But he misses!

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.890
Yabuki's off balance!

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.470
This is Carlos' chance!

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:10.950
<i>Come on!</i>

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.070
Carlos! It's a trap!

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:16.400
Joe wants to pull off his stunt from the first round again!

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:27.290
I see now! He intentionally got off-balance to lure Carlos to the ropes!

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:30.540
Yabuki's demonstrating some astounding cunning here!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.210
Carlos Rivera just barely managed to avoid danger!

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.500
Hey, don't give me that look.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:40.640
Guess this just means I'll have to switch up my game.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.140
But you set up the trap anyway.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.600
Why don't you see it through, Joe?

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.940
Come again?

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.270
You want to go down like a rag doll again, Carlos?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.310
We'll see about that.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.360
Carlos! No!

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.860
<i>Come on!</i>

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.580
Joe!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.970
Get back to a neutral corner!

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.020
Not bad...

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.310
Señor Carlos...

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:22.570
Rivera...

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.830
Well, don't just stand there, ref! Call the match back in!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.130
Yes... R-Right away...

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:48.300
Fight!

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:53.970
Stop!

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.600
Saved by the bell...

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.860
Get it together, Yabuki. This fight's just getting started.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.320
Don't be too hasty.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:09.370
And one more thing...

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.950
Joe, are you all right?

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.550
Joe? Joe, what happened? What's so funny?

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:34.810
Old man, do you think that when Joe fell out of the ring, he...

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:36.850
What're you talking about, dumbass?

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:40.320
What do you think Carlos just told me?

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:45.400
He said that he was bored of petty gimmicks, like elbow blows and rope-a-dopes.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:51.450
He wants to have a great big fight with me, with no gimmicks.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:54.160
I tell you, he's gone and stolen my heart all over again!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.750
S-Simultaneous hits! This is getting dangerous!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:45.540
It's a dual exchange in the middle of the ring right after the bell!

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.100
N-Now I didn't see this happening!

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:24.330
They've rooted themselves in the center of the ring,

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.130
without even trying to dodge each other's punches,

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:29.500
simply hitting each other with all their strength...

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.560
As if trying to test each other's strength...

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:40.100
As if trying to test their own strength...

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.440
Carlos and Yabuki...

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:45.940
are simply... simply... simply...

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:19.430
Stop!

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.820
Hey! Break it up, both of you!

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.830
Carlos! The bell's already rung!

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.330
Joe! Are you trying to get yourself killed?

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.750
That's enough! Stop it!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.750
<i>I've seen enough!</i>

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.980
Cut it out!

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:57.010
Hey, Carlos... It's gotten noisy all of a sudden, hasn't it?

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.390
Who cares about that, Joe...

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:03.510
We don't need a bell for our fight.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.520
Glad we understand each other, Carlos.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.270
Yeah, Joe.

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:23.330
This isn't boxing anymore.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:27.040
It's long since exceeded the petty bounds of boxing!

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:33.050
It's exceeded those bounds into something greater...

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:34.130
Something much greater...

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.510
I don't care what they say!

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:59.000
You're the real world champions!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.050
Yeah! You're the kings of the square jungle!

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.510
Well done, Yabuki Joe!

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:05.010
Well done, Carlos!

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.470
Bravo, Yabuki!

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.700
Bravo, Carlos!

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:38.100
Yabuki! Yabuki! Yabuki!

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:38.100
<i>Carlos! Carlos! Carlos!</i>

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:00.360
I wish you could've been here to see that fight, Rikiishi-kun.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.410
The man you risked everything for, Yabuki Joe,

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.800
truly is an amazing man.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.920
Thinking about Rikiishi?

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.290
Rikiishi, huh...

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:26.300
I'll bet you he's complaining to the Devil in the depths of Hell right now...

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:31.760
saying something like "I want to fight Carlos myself."

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.870
Oh, there he is!

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:52.960
Just look at him!

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:57.460
He vanished from his waiting room, just so he could come here and flirt!

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:59.120
Hey, Joe!

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.840
Let him be.

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:03.030
He's just fought the fight of his life.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:05.300
He's entitled to some peace now.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.800
A piece of what?

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.390
No, he said "peace," not "a piece"!

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:11.100
What do you mean by "peace"?

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:12.590
Uh...

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:18.440
Now why don't we get on home, and get the party ready?

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:20.560
Let's go buy a mountain of delicious food!

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.900
Does that include cream puffs?

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:23.820
Of course it does!

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.360
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.700
Now, keep it down...

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.030
Hey, come on!

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.620
Let's go, Noriko-han.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.750
A-All right...

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:43.420
First Rikiishi, now Carlos...

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:49.220
This is the second time I've truly been lit aflame in this tiny square jungle.

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:52.550
And none of this would have happened if it weren't for you.

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:56.560
Thank you. Thank you from the bottom of my heart.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.380
Wait, Yabuki-kun!

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.870
I can drive you to Namida Bridge in my car!

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.630
Yabuki-kun!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.970
Well, Carlos, it's time we headed back to Venezuela.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:38.360
It's too bad we couldn't say goodbye to Joe Yabuki since it'd spoil their moment.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.230
No, I don't think it's a shame.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.360
Joe Yabuki is now my closest friend.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.360
And true friends don't need to say goodbye,

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.450
because they're always in your heart.

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.400
<i>¡Bravo, el niño!</i> <i>¡Buena suerte, Joe!</i>

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:21.310
Hey!

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:21.970
Ow!

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.480
Don't touch those until Joe gets back!

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:28.480
Yeah, but isn't Bro Joe a little late?

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.980
You're right. He's a little too late.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:35.370
Old man, you think I should drive out and look for him?

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:39.310
It's a car! I bet that's Joe!

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:40.500
Hey, Joe!

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.430
Joe-

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:47.960
Good evening.

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:54.970
Are you here alone, Miss?

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.470
He's left on a journey.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:04.020
I tried to stop him, but he's gone.

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:10.980
He left this with me... to give to you.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:14.690
"Old man, I'm going on a journey again.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:19.910
There's no special reason for it, I just felt like it.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:21.410
Sachi...

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.910
Kinoko...

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.460
Tonkichi...

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:25.950
Taro...

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.460
Hyoromatsu...

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:31.050
You may all be dirty brats, but you're still adorable and special.

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.290
Take care.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.680
And Nishi and Nori-chan,

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:36.140
hurry up and get married..."

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:39.200
Wh-What the hell is he talking about?

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.730
"And old man,

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:46.650
you decrepit alcoholic one-eyed badger..."

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:53.610
I may have caused you nothing but trouble, but let's just say it was mutual.

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:56.820
The only thing bothering me now,

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:01.710
is that you said you had hopes for me to take on the world.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:05.870
Sorry, but becoming world champion just isn't for me.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.040
It's just not my thing.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.260
I hope you'll forgive me.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:27.600
Well, guys,

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.100
guess this is goodbye.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.570
Maybe we'll meet again if we're lucky.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:34.060
Sayonara.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:36.280
So long.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:38.070
Farewell.{auf wiedersehen, goodbye!}

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:13.560
Joe!

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:21.320
Joe!

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.660
Th-This isn't fair...

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.080
You can't just leave without saying a word to me...

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:32.550
That's not... That's not...

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:49.980
Sachi...

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:49.980
<i>Jackass...</i>

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:51.220
No!

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.330
Dammit! Dammit!

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.250
Why the hell did Bro Joe have to leave?

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:13.250
Yeah! Why'd he have to leave?

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.960
Why'd you have to leave, Joe?

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.640
Yabuki-kun...

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:28.100
What a guy...

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:33.560
Yabuki-kun must've been a vagabond ever since he was born.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:38.440
And he was only with us for a short while by chance.

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:46.910
No! He'll be back!

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:49.540
He may be trying to act tough now,

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:54.880
but I know better than anyone that he's lonely, shy, and one hell of a crybaby!

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:56.830
He'll be back!

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.000
He'll come back to Namida Bridge!

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:01.430
There's no way he wouldn't come back!

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:05.180
He'll be back!

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:07.810
I swear he'll be back!

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:10.260
He'll be back, I know it!

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:12.230
When the wind blows back this way,

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:15.060
he'll come striding in with the sunset at his back.

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:16.650
He'll be back!

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:21.360
Today, Yabuki Joe will keep living life to the fullest,

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:23.650
as long as there is a tomorrow...

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:26.200
As long as he is Tomorrow's Joe!
